{"purpose":"Define the product requirements for the EKA ecosystem.","content":"1. eka-standard — the canonical specification (the extensionless EKA file plus the specification/ directory), the single source of truth for the EKA Standard. 2. eka-core — the Go library implementing the standard: identity model, state taxonomy, knowledge/engineering domains, canonical tokens, exchange, and conformance rules. 3. eka-cli — the CLI consumer: validate, init, sync, get, context, and the executable plugin contract. 4. eka-mcp — the AI-agent integration: an MCP server, the AI skill pack, and the CLI plugin. Dependency direction is one-way: eka-standard -\u003e eka-core -\u003e eka-cli and eka-mcp (no cycles; eka-core stays independent of its consumers). Versioning: the standard uses a two-component scheme (major.minor); the tools use semver. Plugin trust: official (maleolabs) plugins are full-trust with checksum verification; third-party plugins require explicit consent and capability review."}